Quavo Confirms Final Migos Album & Tour With Offset Is in the Works: &#8216;We Going to Do It&nbsp;Right&#8217;

Quavo & Offset Reunite in the Studio After Fueling Migos Album&nbsp;Speculation

Offset stopped by DJ Whoo Kid&#8217;s SiriusXM Shade 45 show on Tuesday (Nov. 10) and talked about attending Quavo&#8217;s QRÖMELIFE album release party in L.A. back in September after Whoo Kidd asked how it felt for them to be speaking again after their falling out around 2022.

&#8220;Blessings, the rebuild is always the best build,&#8221; Offset began. &#8220;I was there to support my brother. S&#8211;t&#8217;s hard. It&#8217;s a time and a place for everything and so we just clicking.&#8221;

When discussing who initiated the conversation, the Migos member revealed that the two had been communicating well before they public knew about it. &#8220;We been talking for a long time. Ya&#8217;ll just ain&#8217;t know,&#8221; he said. It just wasn&#8217;t for the world to know. We had to heal behind the scenes, which we still ain&#8217;t heal but we had to heal behind the scenes. It&#8217;s building with your family. Some stuff don&#8217;t go out the house.”

Takeoff&#8217;s death at age 28 in November 2022 helped bring the childhood friends back together again, as they used grief as a common bond.

“I feel like it eased it a little bit,” Quavo said on Complex’s Idea Generation in September when discussing how Take’s death changed their relationship. “I felt like it threw out all the things that I was upset about or that we had friction about. &#8230; I feel like it was it was enough just for me to say, ‘All right, cool. Whatever.’&#8221;

Offset was featured on QRÖMELIFE , and the two plan on making one last Migos album in honor of Takeoff and going on tour together.

